Checkpoint. Does seats.get("Ada") compile on a HashMap<String, u32>?
   yes, because String: Borrow<str> -> Some(3)

There and back: to_owned goes out, borrow comes home
   "Ada"     -> String  -> &str   "Ada"
   [3, 1]    -> Vec     -> &[i32] [3, 1]
   notes.txt -> PathBuf -> &Path  "notes.txt"

A Cow<str> lends a &str from either arm
   Cow::Borrowed -> "ballot", Cow::Owned -> "ballot"

std hands you a Cow when it may have to repair the text
   CStr::to_string_lossy("thanksfish")  -> Cow::Borrowed, "thanksfish"
   CStr::to_string_lossy(b"caf\xe9")    -> Cow::Owned, "caf�"
   String::from_utf8_lossy(valid UTF-8) -> Cow::Borrowed, "café"

The write: to_mut calls to_owned only while the Cow is still Borrowed
   before to_mut: Cow::Borrowed, points at the literal: true
   after to_mut:  Cow::Owned, new buffer: true, capacity == length: true
   to_mut again:  Cow::Owned, same buffer, nothing copied: true
   push('!'): no spare capacity, so the String had to reallocate: true
   the literal is untouched: "Hello World", the Cow reads "Hello World!"
